PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — store LatticeBeam by value (U18 ingest half).

Lattice keeps std::vector<LatticeBeam::Ptr>: one make_shared (control block +
~64 B object) and one pointer chase per beam. LatticeBeam is a value type with
no polymorphism and no shared ownership anywhere in the runtime; value storage
removes the per-beam allocation (SK-0.3: 20.9 of 39.2 ns/beam ingest is
C++-side allocation) and makes the beam array contiguous — the seam a GPU
upload needs (32 B/beam as a vec4 pair). Class 0 by construction: identical
values, identical iteration order; the picovoxel G0 gates hold unchanged.

